title: Transient Command Execution via systemd-run
id: ac8d7dbc-265a-4bd5-a1b8-d91041ee7983
status: experimental
description: Detects use of systemd-run to launch a transient unit, which executes a command under systemd with elevated context and can obscure the parent relationship, a lesser-known execution technique.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1569/
logsource:
  product: linux
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    Image|endswith: '/systemd-run'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '--scope'
      - '-t'
      - '--uid'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - User
  - Image
falsepositives:
  - Administrators using systemd-run
level: medium
tags:
  - attack.execution
  - attack.t1569
